    {
      "sectionTitle": "Configure your audit logs ingestion",
      "sectionText": "1. Select the logs origin.\n  - **To use demo logs**, select *Demo logs* and select *dataiku-managed-storage* connection. It lets you explore the features of the solution. \n  - **To use cloud instance logs**, select *Cloud logs* and select *dku-audit-log* connection as explained [here](https://doc.dataiku.com/dss/latest/operations/audit-trail/dataikucloud.html#access-instances-audit-logs).\n  - **To use Event Server logs**, select *Event Server logs* and select the connection to the location of your [Event Server logs](https://doc.dataiku.com/dss/latest/operations/audit-trail/eventserver.html).\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n2. **For production setup** requiring regular refresh, it is strongly recommended to configure the partitioning section. The smaller the partition period is, the faster and more responsive your monitoring experience will be.\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n3. Click on **RECONFIGURE** to apply your changes.",
